    "title": "Local cultural center hosts free 1776-themed Halloween event - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Noelle Horn ,\n1 hours ago By Pedal to the Stock The Troy-Hayner Cultural Center will host its free family Halloween event, Boo Bash 2026, on Saturday, Oct. 24.\nThis year’s gathering features a 1776 theme offering games, crafts, and kid-friendly Halloween stories.\nThe Boo Bash began in 2014 during a year-long celebration marking the 100th anniversary of the Hayner Mansion.\nTRENDING STORIES:\nLocated in Troy, the cultural center is supported by citizens of the Troy City School District through a local tax levy and contributions to the Friends of Hayner.\nAs part of the themed activities, children can participate in a patriotic checklist featuring historic events such as the Boston Tea Party and the midnight ride of Paul Revere.\nParticipants who complete the activity list will receive a prize and an opportunity to sign the Declaration of Independence.\nThe Troy-Hayner Cultural Center is located at 301 W. Main St. in Troy.",
    "summary": "1 hours ago By Pedal to the Stock The Troy-Hayner Cultural Center will host its free family Halloween event, Boo Bash 2026, on Saturday, Oct. 24. This year’s gathering features a 1776 theme offering games, crafts, and kid-friendly Halloween stories. The Boo Bash began in 2014 during a year-long celebration marking the 100th anniversary of the Hayner Mansion. As part of the themed activities, children can participate in a patriotic checklist featuring historic events such as the Boston Tea Party and the midnight ride of Paul Revere.",
